// Lab 03 (optional path): populate Locations from a OneLake shortcut to the Lakehouse table
// `locations` created by the reference-data notebook.
// 1. In the KQL database: New > OneLake shortcut > Microsoft OneLake > RailLakehouse > Tables > locations
// 2. Run the command below (the shortcut is queried with external_table()).
.set-or-replace Locations <|
    external_table("locations")
    | project stanox = tostring(stanox), tiploc = tostring(tiploc), crs = tostring(crs), nlc = tostring(nlc), name = tostring(name), lat = toreal(lat), lon = toreal(lon)
